Select the Kandelo POSIX target without claiming Linux identity.

This is a target port, not a workaround for an upstream runtime defect.
Recognize wasm32-unknown-kandelo in config.sub and Mozilla's target model;
keep the SDK's real wasm CPU and Unix/POSIX environment. XP_UNIX selects
Mozilla's POSIX implementations, including real pthreads; WASI's noop
thread implementation is not selected. Keep Linux-only paths unselected.

Retain the upgrade's Rust wasm32-unknown-unknown mapping, atomics and
custom getrandom backend. No new kernel/host interface or ABI is added.
Apply after the pinned ESR153 upgrade patches. Target configuration and
all runtime behavior still require qualification; patch application alone
is not that evidence.

